{
  "note": [
    "Strip Near Relay's fabric (DR-106), cut from the one computer layout in scripts/fabric-computer.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. STRIP-NEAR-RELAY v1: the north section of the strip, a bare 8.0 m deck 1.0 m thick, the eye on its centre line 40 m north of Strip Near Station's. No shell, walls, lamps or sky: the black void is the package's own lighting.fog (black, 8 to 16 m), which the engine makes the fog and the background, and the fill is its sourceless lighting.fill. Past 16 m everything is black. The microbe and the speck are overlays and are not in the fabric.",
    "North, 6.0 m off, the deck runs into the foot of the featureless wall: one flat dark face across the whole north, running up, down, left and right out of sight. West, the edge and the void. South, the deck on into Middle of Strip's section and the black.",
    "East, the micro-relay: its 6.0 x 4.0 west face on the strip's east edge 4.0 m from the eye, the case 5.0 m deep, standing on a plinth of its own whose column runs down into the void. The case is drawn red on five sides with its west face open behind a red rim, so the contact inside shows -- the painting makes that face the transparent red plastic it is. The contact is 1.5 m inside the face and 1.2 m north of the eye's line: a post with a pad and an armature above it. SEALED (RELAY in STRIP-NEAR-RELAY and COMPUTER-FIXED != true): the armature held 0.9 m off the post -- the gap the speck overlay fills. CLOSED (COMPUTER-FIXED == true): the armature down on the post. SHATTERED (not RELAY in STRIP-NEAR-RELAY): no case, a heap of red shards on the plinth and the bare post. No label or number anywhere."
  ],
